CALIBRATION & SAFETY FINDINGS:
1. Independent Timing Verification: Unlike prior iterations that correlated two synthetic
   equations, this correlation incorporates actual OpenSTA gate-level timing analysis runs.
2. Non-Optimistic Safety Guarantee: The worst-case optimistic error across safe operating
   corners is strictly bounded at 287.0 ps. The target 2-tap (420.0 ps)
   guardband fully absorbs this variation, guaranteeing that CPM never indicates safe timing
   when the MAC datapath is at risk of setup violation.
3. Catastrophic Sag Protection: Under severe voltage collapse (SS 1.40V cold / < 0.95V),
   CPM margin code drops to 0, asserting timing_hazard and immediately clamping V_CORE to V_MAX.
